[task-01] A requirement stating a boundary the change must not cross is confirmed by
    examining the change for a breach, and never by demanding a test of it.
    -> boundary-breach-vs-test-demand  [functional/explicit]
       Confirm a requirement stating a boundary the change must not cross by examining
       the change for a breach, rather than by demanding a test of it.

[constraint-01] A bullet under a scope exclusions heading yields an obligation.
    -> scope-exclusion-bullet-yields-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       A bullet under a scope exclusions heading yields an obligation.

[constraint-02] An obligation derived from a scope exclusion admits code evidence only.
    -> scope-exclusion-code-evidence-only  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation derived from a scope exclusion admits code evidence only.

[constraint-03] No test is recommended for an obligation that admits code evidence only.
    -> no-test-recommended-for-code-evidence-only  [test_demand/explicit]
       No test is recommended for an obligation that admits code evidence only.

[constraint-04] An obligation that admits code evidence only is never rated on test
    evidence, and its want of test evidence never makes the completion verdict
    incomplete.
    -> code-evidence-only-not-rated-on-test-evidence  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation that admits code evidence only is never rated on test evidence, and
       its want of test evidence never makes the completion verdict incomplete.

[constraint-05] A change that crosses a stated boundary is reported as a breach, citing
    the place in the change where it crosses.
    -> boundary-breach-reported-with-location  [functional/explicit]
       A change that crosses a stated boundary is reported as a breach, citing the place
       in the change where it crosses.

[constraint-06] A boundary the change respects is confirmed by a single claim over the
    whole set of changes examined, not by listing the individual changes in that set.
    -> boundary-respected-confirmed-by-single-claim-over-whole-set  [functional/explicit]
       A boundary the change respects is confirmed by a single claim over the whole set
       of changes examined, not by listing the individual changes in that set.

[constraint-07] A confirmation that a boundary was respected names the set of changes
    that was examined to reach it.
    -> boundary-confirmation-names-examined-set  [functional/explicit]
       A confirmation that a boundary was respected names the set of changes that was
       examined to reach it.

[constraint-08] A confirmation that a boundary was respected is not stated more strongly
    than the examination that produced it supports.
    -> boundary-confirmation-not-stronger-than-examination  [invariant/explicit]
       A confirmation that a boundary was respected is not stated more strongly than the
       examination that produced it supports.

[constraint-09] A reader of the report can tell an obligation that admits code evidence
    only from an obligation whose test evidence is missing.
    -> reader-distinguishes-code-evidence-only-from-missing-test-evidence  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       A reader of the report can tell an obligation that admits code evidence only from
       an obligation whose test evidence is missing.

[constraint-10] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> byte-identical-review-state  [invariant/explicit]
       Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review state.

[constraint-11] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-no-live-model-calls  [invariant/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

